{{!--
    One Thread on the Requirements view.

    A BUTTON, not a box. This diagram answers exactly one question — what waits
    on what — and cannot answer any other: there is no bar on a card, no mode, no
    way to push it. So the reader's next question is always about the row itself,
    and the only way to reach it was to switch tab and find it by eye among nine.
    Pressing a card goes back to the list with that Thread's name already in the
    search box, which both answers the question and shows its working: the box
    says why the list is short, and clearing it puts everything back.

    Five attributes, each with a job:
      data-requires     the drawn ids this one waits on, read by the edge drawing
      data-chain        the piece of work it belongs to, read by the search filter
      data-search       what the box matches on, lowercased when it was built
      data-thread-name  what the box is FILLED with when the card is pressed.
                        The projected name and not the id, because the box
                        matches text a reader can see — so a masked Thread hands
                        over its mask, and finds itself by it.
--}}
<button type="button"
        class="rsr-graph-card{{#if this.masked}} is-masked{{/if}}{{#if this.isConcluded}} is-concluded{{/if}}{{#if this.isLocked}} is-locked{{/if}}"
        data-action="findThread"
        data-node-id="{{this.id}}"
        data-thread-name="{{this.name}}"
        data-requires="{{this.requires}}"
        data-chain="{{this.chain}}"
        data-search="{{this.search}}"
        data-tooltip="{{localize 'RSR.graph.cardHint'}}">
    <span class="rsr-graph-name">{{this.name}}</span>

    {{!-- A requirement that is not on this screen. Marked rather than drawn,
          because an arrow would point at the space the hidden Thread would have
          occupied, and the reader can count columns. Its own tooltip, which wins
          over the card's while the pointer is on it: what this mark means is a
          more urgent question than where the card leads. --}}
    {{#if this.hasUnknown}}
    <span class="rsr-graph-unknown" data-tooltip-class="rsr-tip"
          data-tooltip="{{localize 'RSR.graph.unknownHint'}}">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-question" inert></i>
        {{localize "RSR.graph.unknown"}}
    </span>
    {{/if}}
</button>
